tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:45:  2. THE MANIFEST MUST NOT VERIFY THE LEDGER INSTEAD OF THE WORK.  gate_offline's F3 note
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:46:     records a pass-2 seat measuring BOTH directions green: delete a selfmutant_one call and
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:47:     leave SM_COVERED intact -> GREEN.  The structural answer here is that THERE IS NO
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:48:     COVERED LIST.  The manifest below carries ONLY the one fact a machine cannot derive --
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:49:     what CLASS an artefact is -- and the wiring is DERIVED, every run, from the gate scripts
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:50:     named in run.sh's GATES array.  The manifest cannot lie about wiring because it never
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:51:     states it, and the derivation PRINTS ITS EVIDENCE (gate_arm.sh:97) so the derivation is
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:52:     auditable rather than trusted.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:53:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:54:WITNESS vs DETECTOR -- THE LINE, AND WHY IT IS NOT SYNTACTIC.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:55:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:56:    A DETECTOR asserts the REPAIRED property: it is GREEN once the defect is gone.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:57:    A WITNESS   asserts the PRE-FIX SYMPTOM:  it is RED   once the defect is gone.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:58:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:59:That is sharp, but no grep can evaluate it.  MEASURED, so this is not a preference:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:60:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:61:  * pit8253_latch_probe.py opens "Rung-3 cold-debugger WITNESS for pitlatch / pitclobber"
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:62:    -- and its rows assert the FIXED behaviour ("R1/R2 fail on the PRE-FIX build"), so by the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:63:    line above it is a DETECTOR.  A self-label grep classifies it wrongly and, worse, then
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:64:    stops asking for a gate.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:65:  * hpcmips_ctor_probe.py and sh4_bsc_width_probe.py are DETECTORS whose docstrings both say
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:66:    "The pre-fix WITNESS ... asserts the SYMPTOM" in prose.  A self-label grep classifies
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:67:    BOTH as witnesses -- and would then demand they never be gated, which is backwards.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:68:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:69:So the class is DECLARED here, by a human, one line each.  The file's own summary line is
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:70:cross-checked as an ADVISORY (SELFLABEL), never as a failure, for the measured reason above.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:71:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:72:WHY GATING A WITNESS IS A FAILURE, not merely pointless -- the tooth in the other direction,
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:73:which the reading seat's recommendation did not name.  A witness goes RED the day its fix
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:74:lands.  Wiring one into the battery converts a successful repair into a red gate with a
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:75:bookkeeping cause: the phantom-regression class this project already names, manufactured on
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:76:purpose.  So witness entries are checked for the ABSENCE of a gate call.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:77:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:78:RETROACTIVE IN DOMAIN, GREEN AT INTRODUCTION.  check_boilerplate.py and check_bugfile_sync.py
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:79:are forward-only BY DATE because retro-failing an archive of hundreds of ledger rows gets the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:80:rule switched off, and a disabled rule is worse than no rule.  That argument does not carry
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:81:here: the domain is a few dozen files in ONE FLAT DIRECTORY, enumerable in full today, and an
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:82:unwired probe has no date to be forward-only about.  A date cutoff would also grandfather the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:83:four files this check exists for, permanently.  So nothing is grandfathered -- and the check is
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:84:still green on the day it lands, because each existing gap is written down as a DATED
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:85:EXEMPTION naming the round that owes it.  Debt that expires, not debt that disappears.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:86:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:87:DATES ARE VALIDATED, NEVER GUESSED.  gate_offline.sh records a malformed exemption date that
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:88:never expired AND still satisfied the coverage check ("ieee_store:2026-8-1", 19 days past,
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:89:sorted as FUTURE).  Here a missing or malformed date is RED and names itself; it is never
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:90:silently treated as unexpired.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:91:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:92:WHAT THIS CANNOT DO, said plainly so a green line is not read as more than it is:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:93:  * it cannot tell whether a gated probe's rows are any good.  gate_offline's selfmutant lane
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:94:    and the vacuity taxonomy are what answer that; this answers only "does anything run it".
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:95:  * it cannot stop a DETECTOR being misfiled as tool to silence the requirement.  The
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:96:    filename tooth below refuses *_probe.py/*_witness.py in that class, which closes the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:97:    cheapest form; a rename defeats it.  What is left is a written lie in a tracked file, and
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:98:    that is the same footing every manifest in this harness stands on.  Said, not hidden.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:99:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:100:*** --selftest IS PART OF THE CHECK, NOT A CONVENIENCE. ***  A gate that cannot be shown to
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:101:go RED is the vacuity class this project names first, and "I ran the mutants once" is a
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:102:remembered grep -- the mrwstore2 shape, where a round's witness left no artefact and a later
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:103:row had to re-cost the work.  `--selftest` applies 18 mutants to COPIES in a temp directory
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:104:(never the repo) and asserts the exit status of each.  It is re-runnable by someone who was
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:105:not there, which is the only kind of measurement that survives.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:106:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:107:Usage:  python check_probe_wiring.py [-v] [--regress DIR] [--today YYYY-MM-DD]
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:108:        python check_probe_wiring.py --selftest [-v]
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:109:Exit 0 and print PROBEWIRING_PASS, or exit 1 and print PROBEWIRING_FAIL.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:110:"""
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:111:import os
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:112:import re
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:113:import subprocess
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:114:import sys
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:115:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:116:HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:117:DEFAULT_REGRESS = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(HERE, "..", "..", "regress"))
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:118:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:119:#  Scripts that are part of the battery but are not in the GATES array: run.sh drives it and
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:120:#  lib.sh is sourced by every gate, so an invocation placed in either really would run.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:121:ALWAYS = ("run.sh", "lib.sh")
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:122:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:123:#  A script argument is only a REPO probe if its directory is the regress dir.  gate_offline
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:124:#  runs `python3 "$ACDIR/selftest_absorb.py"` on a MUTATED COPY in the log dir -- counting
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:125:#  that as "the repo file is gated" would be the absorb-control mutant vouching for the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:126:#  artefact it was built to attack.  Anything else is reported under IGNORED rather than
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:127:#  dropped, so a legitimate new spelling shows up as a line to read instead of a silent red.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:128:HERE_DIRS = ("", ".", "$HERE", "${HERE}")
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:129:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:130:CLASS_DETECTOR = "detector"
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:131:CLASS_WITNESS = "witness"
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:132:CLASS_TOOL = "tool"
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:133:CLASS_RESEARCH = "research"
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:134:#  #471: a NON-SHIPPING artefact preserved as EVIDENCE, not as a test.  It exists so a
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:135:#  measurement can be re-run or audited; it is not owed a gate and must not be read as
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:136:#  an unwired detector.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:137:#
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:138:#  *** THIS CLASS EXISTS BECAUSE THE OBVIOUS FIX WOULD HAVE BROKEN SOMETHING. ***  Making
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:139:#  the scan recursive immediately pulls in the instruments preserved beside a kill table
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:140:#  under regress/artifacts/.  A `_probe.py` suffix trips the MISFILED rule if they are
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:141:#  called tools, while calling them detectors demands a gate they should never have --
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:142:#  a file with no honest class.  A farmed seat found this and said plainly: land the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:143:#  complete path-aware fix WITH this classification, or do not land it at all.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:144:CLASSES = (CLASS_DETECTOR, CLASS_WITNESS, CLASS_TOOL, CLASS_RESEARCH)
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:145:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:146:#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:147:#  THE MANIFEST.  One line per python artefact in regress/.  The CLASS is the only thing a
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:148:#  machine cannot derive; the wiring is derived below and printed with its file:line.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:149:#
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:150:#  Adding a probe means adding a line here, deliberately -- the same idiom as run.sh's
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:151:#  GATE_MANIFEST and gate_offline's SM_COVERED.  An unlisted file is RED, so a new detector
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:152:#  cannot arrive unnoticed, which is exactly how all four debts below arrived.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:153:MANIFEST = {
