tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:733:    #
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:734:    #  *** IT USES chr(92) FOR THE BACKSLASH ON PURPOSE AND SAYS SO IN ITS OWN HEADER. ***
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:735:    #  The first attempt hand-typed the escape and the C string literal was split by a REAL
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:736:    #  newline cooked in through the Bash -> heredoc -> Python path -- `error: missing
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:737:    #  terminating " character'.  Keeping this file is what stops the next round
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:738:    #  rediscovering that.
