tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:785:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:786:    #  sgidewidth PASS 2, 2026-08-31.  The measuring seat's nine-build re-measurement of a
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:787:    #  SHIPPED detector, which found two 25/25 escapes the round had missed.  CLASS_RESEARCH:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:788:    #  evidence, not detectors the battery owes a run.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:789:    #
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:790:    #  *** `probe_frozen.py` IS THE POINT OF THIS SET AND MUST NOT BE PRUNED. ***  The seat
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:791:    #  froze the shipped cb28a6f probe before mutant 1 -- and the repo copy WAS EDITED LIVE
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:792:    #  UNDER ITS RUN by the main loop (22 -> 25 -> 29 rows).  Without the frozen copy every
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:793:    #  score in that table would be against a moving instrument, which is exactly the hazard
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:794:    #  the frozen-copy rule exists for, observed rather than hypothesised.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:795:    #
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:796:    #  `mutate4.py` builds the VERBATIM pre-fix arm -- floor clauses (a) and (b) -- and is
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:797:    #  kept because no earlier artifact showed that measurement: 14/25, eleven rows red.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:798:    "artifacts/sgidewidth/opus_p2_20260831/probe_frozen.py":
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:799:        (CLASS_RESEARCH, "sgidewidth pass-2 FROZEN detector -- the shipped cb28a6f probe, held still while the worktree copy moved under the run"),
