tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1103:    "artifacts/gdromcondlies/witness_20260830/gdrom_cond_witness.py": (CLASS_WITNESS,
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1104:                                    "gdromcondlies rung-3 on the unmodified -E dreamcast: "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1105:                                    "one guest mov.w per site ends the host at both live "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1106:                                    "BADVAL exits (GDROM_UNKNOWN_0x88 != 0xb, GDROM_COND "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1107:                                    "unmodelled), 15/15 on the committed build before any "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1108:                                    "edit.  Carries BOTH mandatory controls plus two the "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1109:                                    "ladder does not require and this result needs: a "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1110:                                    "DEVICE-SIGNATURE row in the strong form (a "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1111:                                    "TRANSFORMATION only the device performs -- the write "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1112:                                    "arm masks to a byte, so 0x1234 to CNTLO reads back "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1113:                                    "0x34, which RAM would not do), and ACCEPT rows.  The "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1114:                                    "accept rows are what pin the defect to the VALUE and "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1115:                                    "therefore to #443 BADVAL, rather than to the offset "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1116:                                    "being unserviceable, which is the already-fixed #461 "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1117:                                    "default-arm defect.  *** ITS ACCEPT ROWS MUST NOT BE "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1118:                                    "CARRIED INTO THE DETECTOR UNCHANGED: they discriminate "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1119:                                    "on SURVIVAL, and the fix makes survival universally "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1120:                                    "green -- a survival oracle at a refusal-effect site is "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1121:                                    "the CHANNEL check's canonical vacuous row.  Named by "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1122:                                    "the fable5 seat on pass 1, before the detector existed."),
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1123:    #  #497 PASS 1, the opus5 seat, 2026-08-30.  CLASS_RESEARCH: these are EVIDENCE preserved
