tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1312:#  DATED, NAMED DEBT -- not a count and not a silent allowlist.  gate_offline.sh MEASURED that
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1313:#  a COUNT pin actively obstructs the shrink it claims to want ("6, shrinking not growing" went
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1314:#  RED at 5).  A date expires; shrinking is green by construction.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1315:#
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1316:#  2026-09-20 matches the fbpending_bound:2026-09-20 deadline already standing in
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1317:#  gate_offline.sh's SM_EXEMPT, so #442's two debts fall due together.  IT IS A PROPOSAL: the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1318:#  owner set the SM dates and set them TIGHTER than the ones proposed, and a deadline nobody
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1319:#  chose is a deadline nobody owns.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1320:#
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1321:#  These are wiring jobs, not design ones -- each probe already prints a verdict token and
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1322:#  exits nonzero on failure.  What each needs is a gate that owns it, its rig preconditions,
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1323:#  and ONE clean gate run proving it green before it ships.  That last part is why they are
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1324:#  exempted here rather than wired here: gate_hygiene's own comments record FOUR probes that
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1325:#  shipped latently RED because the commit that added them never fired the gate.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1326:EXEMPT = {
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1327:    #  pit8253_latch_probe.py's exemption is DISCHARGED, 2026-08-30 -- it is now wired into
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1328:    #  gate_arm.sh beside footbridge_sites_probe.py, which is the home gate_hygiene.sh's own
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1329:    #  bump note named for it ("wants an operator who can run that gate").  The entry is
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1330:    #  DELETED rather than dated forward, in the SAME edit that added the wiring, because a
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1331:    #  wired probe that keeps an exemption is a STALE EXEMPTION and this checker reds on it.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1332:    #  Seven exemptions remain.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1333:    #  sh4_bsc_width_probe.py's exemption is DISCHARGED, 2026-08-30 -- wired into
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1334:    #  gate_sh_rounding.sh, whose `-E landisk` machine it already used.  Deleted in the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1335:    #  SAME edit as the wiring, because a wired probe that keeps an exemption is a
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1336:    #  STALE EXEMPTION.  Six exemptions remain.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1337:    "fbpending_drain_probe.py": ("2026-09-20",
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1338:                                 "REPORT-ONLY by default: EXPECT_CAP must be set before a "
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1339:                                 "gate row can mean anything, so wiring is a design step first"),
