tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1570:#  STANDALONE WORDS ONLY.  The first draft used a plain substring and reported
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1571:#  mips_fold_probe.py as self-labelled "witness" -- its summary line reads "the MIPS
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1572:#  fold-witness COUNTERS", where the word names a counter, not the artefact.  That is the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1573:#  substring trap in the one place in this file that was allowed to be a heuristic, and an
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1574:#  advisory that cries wolf is an advisory nobody reads.  MEASURED: with the hyphen guard
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1575:#  the noise line disappears and pit8253's real disagreement still fires.
