tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1580:def domain(regress):
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1581:    """The .py artefacts this check governs, and (mode, why) describing how it decided.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1582:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1583:    *** COMMITTED-OR-STAGED, NOT "ON DISK", AND THE FIRST VERSION HAD IT WRONG. ***  The
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1584:    first draft enumerated the directory, and MINUTES AFTER IT WAS WRITTEN a concurrent
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1585:    round dropped `sgi_eaddr_probe.py` into regress/ as untracked in-flight work.  This
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1586:    check went red -- correctly identifying a real unwired detector, but firing at a
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1587:    file its author had not yet offered for commit, in someone else's working tree.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1588:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1589:    `git ls-files` reads the INDEX, so a probe enters the domain the moment it is `git
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1590:    add`ed -- which is precisely when "every COMMITTED detector" starts to apply, and
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1591:    precisely when the author is present to classify it.  A scratch probe that is never
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1592:    staged defends nothing in a fresh clone either, so it is honestly out of scope.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1593:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1594:    FALLBACK IS ANNOUNCED, NEVER SILENT.  Outside a work tree (the --selftest copies)
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1595:    git cannot answer, and a fallback that quietly changes what a check governs is the
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1596:    kind of silent scope change this harness keeps being bitten by.  So the mode is
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1597:    printed on the summary line.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1598:    """
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1599:    try:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1600:        p = subprocess.run(["git", "ls-files", "--", "*.py"], cwd=regress,
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1601:                           capture_output=True, text=True)
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1602:        if p.returncode == 0:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1603:            #  #471: NO `"/" not in f` FILTER.  Its docstring always claimed "every
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1604:            #  committed DETECTOR under regress/", and the filter made that false --
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1605:            #  the checker could not see below top level, which is exactly where
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1606:            #  #465 shipped a detector that no gate ran.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1607:            #
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1608:            #  `git ls-files` yields paths RELATIVE to regress/, so a top-level file
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1609:            #  still arrives as a bare basename and every existing MANIFEST key keeps
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1610:            #  matching unchanged.  Only nested files gain a path key.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1611:            files = sorted(f for f in p.stdout.split()
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1612:                           if f.endswith(".py")
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1613:                           and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(regress, f)))
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1614:            if files:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1615:                return files, "tracked-or-staged"
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1616:    except OSError:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1617:        pass
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1618:    #  #471: the FALLBACK must descend too.  Leaving it flat would re-create the blind
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1619:    #  spot on any machine where git cannot answer -- a check whose coverage depends
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1620:    #  on which branch it took is the shape this file exists to refuse.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1621:    found = []
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1622:    for dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(regress):
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1623:        dirnames[:] = [d for d in dirnames if d not in (".git", "__pycache__")]
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1624:        for f in filenames:
