tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1647:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1648:#  =======================================================================================
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1649:#  SELFTEST.  Mutants are applied to COPIES in a temp dir; nothing in the repository is
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1650:#  touched, so no .MUTANT sentinel is needed.  EXIT STATUS IS TAKEN FROM THE PROCESS: this
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1651:#  project lost a whole battery result to `cmd | tail`, which reports tail's status, so a
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1652:#  KILLED run read as exit 0.  subprocess.run(...).returncode cannot make that mistake.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1653:#
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1654:#  A CHECKER-SOURCE MUTANT THAT DOES NOT APPLY EXACTLY ONCE IS A FAULT, NEVER A PASS --
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1655:#  absorb_census.py's rule, and it is what keeps this selftest from silently going vacuous
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1656:#  after someone reformats the manifest below.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1657:#
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1658:#  *** AND IT FIRED ON ITS OWN AUTHOR, FIRST RUN. ***  The mutants below started life as
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1659:#  plain string literals, which meant the text they searched for existed TWICE in this file:
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1660:#  once in the manifest and once in the selftest.  _st_apply refused ("x2 ... want 1") rather
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1661:#  than mutating both, which would have silently mutated the selftest instead of the subject.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1662:#  So every mutant target is BUILT from its parts and never written out whole.
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1663:def _lit(*parts):
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1664:    """Join fragments, so the assembled search string appears nowhere in this source."""
tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1665:    return "".join(parts)
