360:#  open", raised the pin, and left the sibling census in the SAME FILE untouched --
361:#  a second red that shipped in the same nine commits and survived the pass that
362:#  was sweeping for exactly this. ***
363:#
364:#  Grandfathered DELIBERATELY, which is one of the two dispositions this gate's own
365:#  message offers ("add prompt detection, or grandfather deliberately").  The
366:#  statement is TRUE rather than convenient: the probe's `session()' drives the
367:#  guest on fixed `settle'/`spin' timeouts and has no prompt predicate at all --
368:#  `grep -c "endswith(" sgi_de_primop_probe.py' is 0.  So it belongs on this list
369:#  exactly as the other seventeen do.
370:#
371:#  ADDING REAL READINESS IS FILED, NOT DONE, and the reason is scope rather than
372:#  difficulty: changing how that probe decides a command finished perturbs all 47
373:#  rows and owes a full re-measured kill table.  That is a round, not a records fix,
374:#  and doing it inside a records pass is how a green detector becomes unverified.
375:GRANDFATHERED_PROMPTLESS="pcc2_width_witness.py pcc2_width_probe.py sgi_de_primop_probe.py drive_guest.py gdrom_data_probe.py gdrom_default_probe.py
376:sh_intprio_probe.py sh_iprbcd_probe.py sh_pclock_probe.py sh_tlbmulti_probe.py
377:asic_badaddr_probe.py wdc_flood_probe.py gdrom_decline_probe.py
378:gdrom_toclen_probe.py wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py wdc_altoffset_probe.py
379:gdrom_cond_probe.py sgi_re_width_probe.py
380:sgi_de_width_probe.py sgi_re_unmapped_probe.py"
381:
382:#  *** THIS WAS THE THIRD POPULATION AND THE F2 EDIT MISSED IT.  Found by the agy seat
383:#  on pass 2. ***  py_code and probe_code were converted to recursive-minus-artifacts
384:#  while this line kept a FLAT GLOB -- so two censuses were aligned and a third was not,
385:#  which is the exact defect F2 exists to end.
386:#
387:#  It AGREES today (recursive-minus-artifacts == flat == 59) and that agreement is a
388:#  COINCIDENCE, not a property: a .py added in any NEW non-artifacts subdirectory would
389:#  be scanned by two censuses and missed by this one.  Equal counts are not an aligned
390:#  population, and reading the equality as safety is how the flat glob survived the
391:#  first repair.
392:_ptylist=$(find "$HERE" -name "*.py" -type f ! -path "$HERE/artifacts/*" 2>/dev/null \
393:           | xargs grep -l "pty.fork" 2>/dev/null | sed "s|.*/||" | sort)
394:_ptyn=$(printf '%s' "$_ptylist" | grep -c . )
395:_promptless=$(cd "$HERE" && printf '%s' "$_ptylist" | tr ' ' '
396:' | xargs grep -L "endswith(" 2>/dev/null | sort)
